    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Refresher stops an app on this TV on a schedule you choose, then opens it again. That is all it does.\n\n•  No account, ads, analytics or tracking.\n•  Nothing is uploaded. The only download is Shizuku itself, from Shizuku\'s own GitHub page, and only if you press Get in Setup. Refresher checks it is signed by Shizuku\'s developer before installing it. Otherwise its only network connection is to this TV itself, for setup.\n•  It can\'t see your files or your accounts. With Shizuku, Home shows the title of music or a show playing in the background and keeps refreshes away from it; that title is never stored or sent. The System page shows how much memory and processor each app uses. It keeps a one-hour history of memory and processor (one reading a minute, on this TV only).\n•  It keeps your rules and a short activity log on this TV, plus a small backup file of app names and intervals.\n•  Remove Refresher\'s setup, under Setup, undoes everything setup changed and deletes the backup.\n\nIt is open source: github.com/TheFactor1/refresher</string>
